# tools/gen/chapter/tigerbeetle_off_by_one_census_witness.rish -- e49 Off-By-One.
#
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/gen/chapter/tigerbeetle_off_by_one_census_witness.rish
#
# Requires gratitude/tigerbeetle submodule present.
# Clean-room: presence only - never copies into rye/.
# Leaf only -- no nested elder choirs.

say "tb-off-by-one: Language EN — off-by-one; index, count, and size stay distinct."
say "tb-off-by-one: Style Radiant — division shows its intent; units stay in the name."
say "tb-off-by-one: Lens TAME — e49 · clean-room study · almanac seat 55."
# AN ABSENT OPTIONAL GITLINK IS A FACT ABOUT THE HOST, NEVER A DEFECT (`20260908.195500`).
# `gratitude/tigerbeetle` is a submodule this tree STUDIES and never links, so a clone that has not
# initialised it is a correct clone. This witness asserted the checkout, which made it permanently
# unrostable: a row for it would red the whole fleet on every machine that had not run
# `git submodule update --init`. That is very likely WHY it was never rostered -- and an unrostered
# witness is one nothing runs, so the hard assert bought a red nobody would ever hear.
#
# THE CENSUS ALREADY ANSWERS IN THREE WAYS and this witness now believes it: exit 2 `verdict=absent`
# (the clone is not here), exit 1 `verdict=thin` (the clone is here and something it must teach is
# missing), exit 0 `verdict=ok`. Only `thin` is a defect. The elder witness read `census.ok`, which
# is false for BOTH 1 and 2, so it could not tell a missing dependency from a real finding.
#
# The failure is asserted as a NEGATIVE on `verdict=thin` rather than nested inside a conditional,
# because `assert X else Y` already owns `else` and cannot sit inside `if ... then`. One assert, and
# it fires on the one answer that means something is wrong.

let census = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/t/tigerbeetle_off_by_one_census.sh"]
say census.out

# invariant: the census reached a verdict at all -- a run that printed none is a broken script
# rather than an honest answer, and it must never read as a skip.
assert census.out contains "verdict=" else "tb-off-by-one: the census printed no verdict at all"

# invariant: the clone, where present, still teaches every law this census reads for. `thin` is the
# only answer that means a defect, and it is the only one that fails here.
assert (census.out contains "verdict=thin") == false else "tb-off-by-one: the clone is present and the census reads THIN -- a law it must teach is missing"

if (census.out contains "verdict=absent") then say "tb-off-by-one: SKIP -- gratitude/tigerbeetle is an uninitialised submodule here; run git submodule update --init gratitude/tigerbeetle to read the census on this host"

say "GREEN: tb-off-by-one -- the census answered, and answered nothing thin."
